WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.350
- [Narrator] Stand on the equator

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:06.350
and you'll be moving at
1,670 kilometers per hour,

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:08.970
faster than the speed of sound.

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:10.660
That's how quickly Earth rotates

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:13.320
on its axis from west to east,

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:16.160
and that rotation is largely responsible

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:18.670
for the distribution of every desert,

00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:22.110
forest, and swamp on the planet.

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:24.210
So, let's do a little experiment.

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:28.500
Let's say we reverse
Earth's rotation, what then?

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:30.360
Well, you'll change a lot more

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:31.460
than just the sunsets.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:37.100
This may seem like a
ridiculous scenario at first,

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:39.920
but scientists have
actually run simulations

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:42.050
for a backward-spinning Earth,

00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:44.790
because it happens to
be a great way to test

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:46.870
how well we can model our planet.

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:51.870
So, let's pretend we have a
big, red button, and presto.

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:55.390
Now, as Earth slows down
to reverse direction

00:00:55.390 --> 00:00:58.130
everything would go flying to the east,

00:00:58.130 --> 00:01:01.520
so the whole process
will leave a huge mess.

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:03.010
But let's take a look at the equator

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:05.760
once Earth has gotten back up to speed.

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:07.460
These are the trade winds,

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:10.820
which normally blow westward
due to Earth's rotation.

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:13.350
So on backwards Earth, they reverse,

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:15.540
and that's where things get interesting.

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:18.720
At first, changes would
be relatively small.

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:21.330
Hurricanes, for example,
would no longer travel

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:24.120
from east to west across the Atlantic,

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:27.370
and westbound flights would
suddenly be much shorter

00:01:27.370 --> 00:01:31.400
compared to eastbound. Not so bad, right?

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:35.760
Let's fast forward a few
thousand years into the future.

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:37.930
Changes in overall rain patterns

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:41.490
would turn Africa's
Sahara Desert from this,

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:44.000
to something more like this.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.300
In fact one simulation estimated

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:48.820
that the deserts of the world would shrink

00:01:48.820 --> 00:01:52.720
from 42 million square
kilometers to 31 million,

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:55.200
providing new plant
life which would absorb

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:57.550
more carbon dioxide from the atmosphere,

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:00.980
potentially offsetting the
extreme warming effects

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:04.570
from climate change. Wow,
maybe we really should

00:02:04.570 --> 00:02:06.300
reverse Earth's rotation.

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:09.460
But hold on, if the trade
winds reverse direction,

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:12.230
it means that other wind
patterns change too,

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:14.110
including the prevailing westerlies

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:16.760
that normally blow east
across the Northern Atlantic,

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:18.610
and bring warm winds from the ocean

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:21.750
to Northwest Europe, keeping winters mild.

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:24.400
But on backwards Earth,
the westerlies reverse,

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:26.320
and instead, Europe is bombarded

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:28.490
with cold winds from Russia.

00:02:28.490 --> 00:02:31.650
As a result, scientists
estimate winter temperatures

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:35.310
would drop by up to 10 degrees Celsius.

00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:38.720
In fact, most of the North
Atlantic would grow colder.

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:40.730
Simulations show that the Gulf Stream,

00:02:40.730 --> 00:02:43.250
which normally transports
warm tropic waters

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:46.450
to the North would reverse and shrink.

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:50.620
In North America, the landscape
would change drastically.

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:54.120
For example the iconic deserts
of the American Southwest

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:56.540
would disappear, and become the deserts

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:58.980
of the Southeast instead.

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:00.510
And while you're  packing up to move

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:03.580
to the beautiful new
green pastures of Arizona,

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:05.270
take a look at the horizon,

00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:08.193
and enjoy that peculiar
sunset to the east.

